# UCF M-next E: both host matrices and the crash/partition suite through `yin.vm.ucf.compose`

**Precondition:** met. `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/compose.cljc` is on the branch with D15a, D15 and D16 landed, and its public surface matches the D15 brief.

**Outcome:** every row below drives only `yin.vm.ucf.compose`, and everything is green on all three lanes and across real JVM and Node processes. Two parts of the contract cannot be built through the composition as it stands; they are named prerequisites below. Some sub-cases are not done and are listed as incomplete. No production edits and no git writes. The work is in `datomworld-stage-e`, not the `datomworld-e` path the brief named.

**Milestone completion does not claim full UCF closure.** Full acceptance waits for every row of 7.11.1, including the post-M5 gates; 14.1 and 14.2 close different gates with independent evidence. E closes clause 10 and the composition halves of clauses 3 and 8, within the limits below. It neither re-closes nor re-opens the M4 kept-cursor gate. It does not make unprotected external IO transactional: 14.2.1's guarantee is admission, not effect atomicity beyond the enrolled boundary. Governance recovery after quarantine, exhaustion or lost authority state stays outside the automatic protocol.

## Changed files (all new, all under `test/yin/vm/ucf/`)

| File | Lines | What it is |
|---|---|---|
| `stage_e_world.cljc` | 1392 | Portable. One "life" of a scenario over a single scratch root holding the durable media: a file authority, `compose/file-journals`, a `dao.jing.file` store and a side log. Each durable medium is wrapped so a named cut fires at an exact boundary: a journal frame, a store put, or a composition tick. Also an interpreter for plain-data life programs, and read-only inspection through `authority/open!` (no reclaim). |
| `stage_e_scenarios.cljc` | 1307 | Portable. 51 scenarios (lives plus checks) and the in-process runner. |
| `stage_e_rows_test.cljc` | 70 | 13 deftests running every scenario in one process. This is the isolated-runtime form on all three lanes. |
| `stage_e_peer.cljc` | 114 | A peer program that runs one life as its own OS process (JVM `-main`, Node `main`). At its cut it prints the event and blocks. |
| `stage_e_process_test.clj` | 310 | JVM harness. It spawns JVM and Node peers and kills them with `destroyForcibly` at the cut (exit 137). |

**Harness rules:**
- The harness builds the Node peer itself on each run, so the gate cannot skip. It uses `compile vm-bench --config-merge` to write `target/stage-e-peer.js`; `shadow-cljs.edn` is untouched.
- It AOT-compiles the JVM peer into a fresh `target/stage-e-classes-<uuid>`.
- No ports, no wall-clock sleeps: waits are bounded deadline polls, and protocol time moves only through clock readings the judge appends as ticks.
- Every process is destroyed in a `finally`.

